Do not introduce near-match colors, spacing values, radii, or shadows when an existing token covers the need.

## Typography

- Use Roboto across all MesaOrigins product screens.
- Use `#0F172A` for headings/titles, `#475569` for primary body text, `#64748B` for secondary text, `#94A3B8` for placeholders/muted text, `#1E40AF` for links/actions, and white on dark or colored surfaces.
- Use the following type scale. Set readable line heights, generally 1.2-1.3 for headings and 1.4-1.6 for body copy.

| Role | Size / weight | Primary use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Display | 28px ExtraBold | KPI values, hero numbers |
| Page title | 24px Bold | Page headings, modal titles |
| Section title | 18px SemiBold | Card headers, section titles |
| Subtitle | 16px SemiBold | Subsections, widget titles |
| Body large | 15px Regular | Important descriptions |
| Body | 14px Regular | Default copy, table cells |
| Body small | 13px Regular | Secondary content, form labels |
| Caption | 12px Regular | Timestamps, helper text, metadata |
| Overline | 11px Medium | Section labels, category tags |
| Micro | 10px Regular | Dense chart labels only |

- Do not use text smaller than 12px for essential mobile content. Use 10-11px only for nonessential chart labels or compact badges when legibility is preserved.
- Use sentence case for labels and headings unless a source label is conventionally uppercase.
- Preserve a clear hierarchy; do not compensate for weak hierarchy with arbitrary colors or font weights.

## Color and accessibility

- Page background: `#F8FAFC`; cards/panels: `#FFFFFF`; table headers and hover backgrounds: `#F1F5F9`; borders/dividers: `#E2E8F0`.
- Primary actions, active navigation, links, and interactive highlights use `#1E40AF`.
- Status UI must use the supplied background + text pair, with the accent for icons or indicators.
- Never communicate status by color alone. Add a text label, icon, pattern, or direct annotation.
- Preserve at least WCAG AA contrast: 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text and meaningful non-text UI.
- Always show keyboard focus with a 2px `#1E40AF` ring or an equivalent accessible focus treatment. Do not remove focus outlines without replacement.

## Desktop dashboard layout

- Desktop sidebar: 260px wide, `#FFFFFF`, right border `#E2E8F0`.
- Sidebar items use icon + label, a 10px gap, and approximately 8px vertical padding. Active items use `#DBEAFE` background with `#1E40AF` text.
- Use a responsive content grid. KPI cards appear in a horizontal row when space allows, with 16-20px gaps.
- Standard card: white background, 12px radius, 1px `#E2E8F0` border, 20-24px padding, no shadow.
- Use 24px between page sections and 32px for major section breaks.
- Avoid fixed desktop canvas widths. `1116px` full-width and `540px` half-width from the source are reference sizes, not required viewport widths.

## Responsive breakpoints

Use content-driven behavior, with these defaults unless the project already defines compatible breakpoints:

| Range | Layout behavior |
| --- | --- |
| `< 640px` | Mobile: one column, 16px page gutter, compact cards |
| `640-767px` | Large mobile: one column; two-column KPI grid only when labels remain readable |
| `768-1023px` | Tablet: 24px gutter, 2-column card grid, drawer or compact navigation |
| `>= 1024px` | Desktop: persistent 260px sidebar and multi-column dashboard |

- Build mobile-first and enhance with `min-width` queries.
- Test at 320px, 375px, 390px, 768px, 1024px, and a wide desktop viewport.
- Prevent page-level horizontal scrolling. Allow horizontal scrolling only inside an intentionally contained data region.
- Respect notches and home indicators with `env(safe-area-inset-*)` for fixed headers, sheets, and bottom navigation.

## Mobile navigation and shell

- Replace the persistent desktop sidebar below 1024px with an accessible drawer or a compact top/bottom navigation pattern suited to information depth.
- Mobile top bar: 48px minimum height, 12–16px horizontal padding, icon-only MesaOrigins mark, concise page title, and only the highest-priority action.
- A navigation drawer should retain the white surface, active Sky/primary treatment, labels, and icons from desktop. It must trap focus while open, close on Escape, restore focus to its trigger, and provide a visible close control.
- Use bottom navigation only for 3-5 stable top-level destinations. Keep it clear of safe areas and show both icon and label.
- Move secondary actions into an overflow menu; do not crowd the top bar.
- Never rely on hover to reveal mobile navigation or controls.

## Mobile spacing and touch

- Use 16px screen gutters on mobile and 24px on tablet.
- Reduce standard card padding from 20-24px to 16px on mobile; use 12px only for dense, secondary cards.
- Stack dashboard sections vertically with 16px gaps; use 24px for major breaks.
- Interactive targets must be at least 44x44 CSS pixels; prefer 48px for primary controls and frequently used industrial workflows.
- Keep at least 8px between adjacent touch targets.
- Mobile text inputs, selects, and search fields should be at least 44px high. Use 16px input text to avoid unintended mobile browser zoom.
- Primary mobile actions may become full-width. Keep destructive actions visually separated and require confirmation when consequences are significant.
- Fixed bottom actions must not cover content; add equivalent bottom padding plus the safe-area inset.

## Cards and KPIs

- Desktop KPI cards use 20-24px padding and a 28px ExtraBold value.
- On mobile, use a single-column card stack by default. A 2-column KPI grid is allowed only when each card remains at least about 156px wide and labels do not truncate ambiguously.
- Keep the 28px KPI value when it fits. Reduce to 24px only when necessary for long values; never below 20px.
- Keep the label, value, unit, trend, and timeframe together. Do not detach context from a metric across scroll positions.
- Prefer wrapping or a shorter approved label over ellipsis for operationally important content.

## Tables and dense data on mobile

- Desktop table header: `#F8FAFC`, 12-13px SemiBold `#475569`.
- Desktop rows: white, 14px vertical padding, 1px `#E2E8F0` divider; cell text 13-14px Regular `#475569`.
- Do not squeeze a many-column desktop table into the viewport.
- Choose one deliberate mobile pattern based on the task:
  - Convert records into stacked cards for scanning and actions.
  - Show the 2-4 highest-priority columns and expose the rest in a details view.
  - Use a contained horizontal scroller when column comparison is essential; keep the key identifier column sticky and provide a visible affordance that more content exists.
- Preserve sorting, filtering, selection, pagination, and row actions in the mobile equivalent.
- Keep headers associated with values for assistive technology. Do not implement a data table as unrelated visual divs without semantics.

## Forms, search, and filters

- Search bar: 40px high on desktop, at least 44px on mobile; 8px radius; 1px `#E2E8F0` border; 2px `#1E40AF` focus ring; 14px placeholder in `#94A3B8`.
- Stack form controls vertically on mobile. Keep labels visible above controls; do not use placeholder text as the only label.
- Use the correct mobile input mode and autocomplete value for numeric, phone, email, date, and search fields.
- Present complex filters in a bottom sheet or full-screen panel on mobile. Show an active-filter count and provide clear Apply and Reset actions.
- Keep validation next to the affected field, explain how to fix it, and move focus to the first invalid field after submission.

## Buttons and badges

- Primary button: `#1E40AF` fill, white text, 8px radius.
- Secondary button: white fill, `#1E40AF` text, 1px `#1E40AF` border.
- Desktop padding: 10px vertical and 16-20px horizontal; 14px Medium text.
- Maintain the 44px minimum touch height on mobile even when visual padding tokens are smaller.
- Status badges: 4-6px horizontal and 2-4px vertical padding, 6px radius, 11-12px Medium, semantic background + text color pair.
- Icon-only buttons require an accessible name and a tooltip for pointer/keyboard users. Do not use an icon whose meaning is unclear without a visible label.

## Charts and data visualization

- Series 1 / production / plan: `#1E40AF`.
- Series 2 / scrap / actual: `#F59E0B`.
- Success / completed: `#10B981`; warning / in progress: `#F59E0B`; error / overdue: `#EF4444`; neutral track and grid: `#E2E8F0`.
- Axis labels: `#94A3B8`; chart titles: `#0F172A`; legend text: `#475569`.
- Chart cards follow the standard card style with 20-24px desktop padding and 16px mobile padding.
- Chart header: title on the left and legend on the right at wide widths. On mobile, wrap or stack the legend below the title; never compress it until labels become unreadable.
- Use horizontal grid lines only, 1px `#E2E8F0`; omit vertical grid lines unless they are necessary for interpretation.
- Full-size bar/line plot height: 180-220px. Mobile plot height: approximately 200-240px when needed for touch and labels.
- Grouped bars: 16px nominal width, 3px intra-group gap, 20px group gap, 4px top-corner radius. Scale bar width/gaps responsively rather than forcing overflow.
- Lines: 2px stroke with filled 8px data points. Increase the invisible pointer/touch hit area without enlarging the visible dot.
- Donut: 100-140px diameter, 70% hollow center, 28px ExtraBold center value, status palette segments, vertically spaced legend.
- Mobile donut charts may place the legend below the centered donut. Keep each legend row at least 44px high if it is interactive.
- For crowded mobile time series, reduce tick frequency, abbreviate labels unambiguously, or use a contained horizontal plot scroller. Do not render overlapping labels.
- Tooltips use 12px Medium text and must work with touch, keyboard, and pointer. Provide persistent labels or a data summary when hover is unavailable.
- Supply a concise accessible chart name and a text/table summary of the values or trend. Do not make the canvas/SVG the only source of information.
- Keep series color assignments stable across chart types and screens.

## Motion, state, and feedback

- Provide explicit loading, empty, error, offline, and permission-denied states for dashboard modules.
- Prefer skeletons or stable placeholders that preserve layout and prevent large shifts.
- Keep interaction feedback fast and subtle. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` and avoid decorative animation in operational flows.
- Do not make a user repeat a completed action because the viewport changed or the device rotated.

## Implementation checklist

Before considering a MesaOrigins screen complete, verify:

- Brand spelling, logo variant, colors, Roboto typography, spacing, and radii match this file.
- Desktop and mobile share the same information hierarchy and functionality.
- The screen works at 320px without accidental horizontal overflow.
- Navigation, dialogs, drawers, sheets, tables, forms, and charts are keyboard and screen-reader usable.
- Touch targets are at least 44x44px and are not crowded.
- Status is not conveyed by color alone and text meets WCAG AA contrast.
- Tables and charts use an intentional small-screen pattern rather than simple shrink-to-fit.
- Loading, empty, error, and long-content states are implemented.
- No arbitrary colors, shadows, type sizes, spacing values, or radii were introduced.
